            <ArticleTitle>The intraocular CD4/CD8 ratio in a black South African patient with Behçet's disease uveitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7196/SAMJ.2016.v107.i1.12039</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 33-year-old black South African male patient was referred to our uveitis service with a 5-year history of panuveitis refractory to treatment. He had an associated history of recurrent mouth and genital ulcers, predating the uveitis history by about 2 years. The measurement of his intraocular CD4/CD8 ratio helped make a diagnosis of Behçet's disease uveitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
